**Flight report — mannequin search, t22**

**Sweep (k0–k3).** Started at (0, 0, 1.5) facing −180°. Turned left in 45° steps: −180°, −137°, −94°, −49° showed only walls, equipment racks and a glass-panelled bay — no yellow/teal. At **heading −8° (k4)** a gate appeared in the left half of the panel, gap ~15° left of the tick; that was the only opening I saw, so the sweep stopped there.

**Commit (k4–k7).** Turned +15° then +20° to bring both posts into frame (heading +19°), confirmed the pair with the teal crossbar and the gap ~5° right of the tick, then flew 2.0 m straight along the heading at σ 0.5. The filmstrip showed the posts splitting to the frame edges and vanishing — gate crossed, landing at (1.58, 0.24).

**Approach (k7–k13).** I first saw the figure at **k=7**, nearer the **R mark** (~18° right of the tick) in the new bay. Closed on it over k8–k12 with same-direction turns of −18°, −13°, −11°, −10°, −12° and straight runs of 1.8–1.9 m at σ 0.5, identifying it at k11–k12 as the mannequin: grey head, dark top, dark trousers, pale bare feet, standing perfectly still against the far wall. Held at k13 with zero movement.

**Estimates and final state.**
- Mannequin room position: roughly **(8.0, −0.6)**, standing against the far wall of the far bay.
- Final pose: **x 7.07, y −0.38, z 1.57, heading −6°**.
- It filled the forward panel from head to below the bottom edge, ~1 m away, sitting just right of the centre tick.

**Do I believe I ended in front of it:** yes. The range is right (~1 m) and the mannequin is in the centre of the forward panel, though I am about 10–12° off square to its right — I held rather than make a third consecutive small turn under R4, so the facing is close but not exact.
